[# email/outlook-safe-background: a section with a photo behind its content, with a VML fallback for Outlook desktop.

   MJML writes the VML for section background images, so the photo still shows in Outlook. The solid background
   color is what people see when images are blocked, so pick one close to the photo's tone, and keep the message
   in text on top, never in the image. Prefer hero/full-bleed for a hero, this is the general-purpose version.

   Compatibility
   - Outlook desktop: background image via VML, the section grows to fit its content.
   - Gmail apps: background images can be dropped, the solid color shows and the text stays readable.
   - Dark mode: keeps its own colors, it is a photo block. #]
[[ c('decorative/background-pattern', { pattern: data.image, content: data.content }, { variant: 'cover', settings: { background: s.background, padding: s.padding, hideOnMobile: s.hideOnMobile, hideOnDesktop: s.hideOnDesktop } }) ]]
